hadiths[35]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17388","Haddathana Ismail ibn Ibrahim, he said akhbarana Ayyub, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar heard that Rafi narrates concerning that a prohibition from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came to him, and I was with him, and asked him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade renting farms. So Ibn Umar left them and did not rent them, and when asked he said: Ibn Khadij claims that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade renting farms."
"17389","Haddathana Sufyan, from Ibn Ajlan, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Pray the dawn in its early brightness, for it is greater for your rewards, or greater for reward."
"17390","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said, from Malik ibn Anas, he said haddathani Rabiah, from Hanzalah ibn Qays, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade renting farms. He said: I said: For gold and silver. He said: No, he only forbade it for part of what comes out of it, as for with gold and silver, there is no harm in it."
"17391","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said, haddathana Muhammad ibn Yusuf, he said I heard al-Saib ibn Yazid ibn Ukht al-Nimr, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst earning is the price of a dog, and the earnings of a cupper, and the dowry of a prostitute."
"17392","Haddathana Yazid, haddathana Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Rafi ibn Khadij, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no cutting for fruit nor for pith."
"17393","Haddathana Yahya, from Sufyan, he said haddathani my father, from Abayah ibn Rifah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from his grandfather Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we will meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives. He said: Hasten, whatever causes blood to flow and the name of Allah is mentioned over it, eat, except tooth and nail. And I will tell you: as for tooth, it is bone, and as for nail, it is the knives of the Abyssinians. He said: And we gained plunder of camels and sheep, and a camel among them fled, so a man shot it with an arrow and restrained it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These camels have wildness like the wildness of wild beasts, so when one overcomes you, do with it like this."
"17394","Haddathana Abu Usamah, he said haddathana al-Walid ibn Kathir, he said haddathana Bushayr ibn Yasar, freedman of Banu Harithah, that Rafi ibn Khadij and Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Muzabanah, fruit for dates, except the owners of Araya, for he permitted them."
"17395","Haddathana Waki, he said haddathana Sufyan, from his father, from Abayah ibn Rifah, from his grandfather Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Dhu al-Hulayfah of Tihamah, and we gained sheep and camels. He said: The people hastened and boiled them in pots, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and ordered them overturned. Then he said: Ten sheep equal a camel. He said: Then a camel fled, and among the people were only a few horses, so a man shot it with an arrow and restrained it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These beasts have wildness like the wildness of wild beasts, so what overcomes you thereof, do with it like this. He said: So Rafi ibn Khadij said: We hope and we fear to meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives, shall we slaughter with reeds. He said: Hasten, whatever causes blood to flow and the name of Allah is mentioned over it, eat, except tooth and nail. And I will tell you about that: as for tooth, it is bone, and as for nail, it is the knives of the Abyssinians."
"17396","Haddathana Waki, he said haddathana Sharik, from Abi Husayn, from Mujahid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hiring land for coined dirhams or for a third or a quarter."
"17397","Haddathana Yazid, haddathana al-Masudi, from Wail Abi Bakr, from Abayah ibn Rifah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from his grandfather Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which earning is purest. He said: The work of a man with his hand, and every blessed sale."
"17398","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from his father, from Abayah ibn Rifah, he said akhbarani Rafi ibn Khadij, he said I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fever is from the blast of Hell, so cool it with water."
"17399","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, he said haddathana Ikrimah, from Abi al-Najashi, freedman of Rafi ibn Khadij, he said I asked Rafian about renting land, I said: I have land I rent. Rafi said: Do not rent it for anything, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever has land, let him plant it, and if he does not plant it, let him give it to his brother to plant, and if he does not, let him leave it. I said to him: What if I leave him and my land, and he plants it then sends me straw. He said: Take nothing from it, not even straw. I said: I did not stipulate with him, he only gifted me something. He said: Take nothing from him."
"17400","Haddathana Abu al-Nadr, he said haddathana Shubah, from Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym, he said I heard Abayah ibn Rifah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij narrating that his grandfather when he died left a slave girl and a water camel and a cupper boy and land. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the slave girl and forbade her earnings, Shubah said: fearing she would fornicate. And he said: Whatever the cupper earns, feed the water camel with it. And he said about the land: Plant it or leave it."
"17401","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir and al-Khuzai, they both said haddathana Sharik from Abu Ishaq from Ata from Rafi ibn Khadij who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Whoever sows in the land of a people without their permission has no share of the crop and his expense is returned to him. Al-Khuzai said what he spent and he has no share of the crop."
"17402","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq who said haddathana Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz from al-Saib ibn Yazid from Rafi ibn Khadij who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said The price of a dog is foul and the dowry of a prostitute is foul and the earnings of a cupper are foul."
"17403","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan, haddathana Rishdin from Yazid ibn Abdullah from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abdullah ibn Amr from Rafi ibn Khadij from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he mentioned Makkah and said Indeed Ibrahim declared Makkah inviolable and I declare inviolable what is between its two lava tracts."
"17404","Haddathana Surayj who said haddathana Fulayh from Utbah ibn Muslim from Nafi ibn Jubayr who said Marwan addressed the people and mentioned Makkah and its sanctity, so Rafi ibn Khadij called out to him and said If Makkah is a sanctuary then Madinah is a sanctuary made sacred by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it is written with us on a Khawlani hide, if you wish that we read it to you we will do so, so Marwan called out to him Yes, that has reached us."
"17405","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said who said haddathana Bakr ibn Mudar from Ibn al-Had from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Rafi ibn Khadij who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Indeed Ibrahim, peace be upon him, declared Makkah sacred and I declare sacred what is between its two lava tracts, meaning Madinah."
"17406","Haddathana Abu Said the freedman of Banu Hashim who said haddathana Abdullah ibn Jafar who said haddathana Uthman ibn Muhammad from Rafi ibn Khadij that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw redness had appeared and disliked it, then when Rafi ibn Khadij died they placed on his bier a red velvet cloth, so the people wondered at that."
"17407","Haddathana Abu al-Mughirah who said haddathana al-Awzai who said haddathana Abu al-Najashi who said haddathani Rafi ibn Khadij who said We used to pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then slaughter a camel which was divided into ten portions, then cooked, and we would eat ripe meat before the sun set. He said And we used to pray Maghrib in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and one of us would leave and he could still see the places of his arrows."
"17408","Haddathana Yunus who said haddathana Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd, haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Bushayr ibn Yasar from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah and Rafi ibn Khadij that Abdullah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisah ibn Masud came to Khaybar for a need of theirs and separated, then Abdullah ibn Sahl was killed and they found him slain. He said Then Muhayyisah and Huwayyisah the two sons of Masud came and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl the brother of the slain came, and he was the youngest of them, and they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he who spoke began with the one most entitled to the blood, though these two were older, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Let the eldest speak. He said Then they spoke concerning their companion. He said Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Establish your right to your companion or your slain by fifty oaths from you. They said O Messenger of Allah, a matter we did not witness, how can we swear. He said Then the Jews exonerate themselves by fifty oaths from them. They said A disbelieving people. He said So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, paid his blood money from his own. He said Then I entered an animal pen of theirs and a she-camel from those camels which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had paid, kicked me with its leg."
"17409","Haddathana Khalaf ibn Hisham who said haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd from Yahya ibn Said from Bushayr ibn Yasar from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah and Rafi ibn Khadij from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"17410","Haddathana Yunus who said haddathana Layth from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman from Hanzalah ibn Qays from Rafi ibn Khadij that he said My uncle told me that they used to lease land in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for what grows on the water channels and something of the crop which the owner of the crop excepted, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that. So I said to Rafi How is leasing it for dinar and dirham. So Rafi said There is no harm in it for dinar and dirham."
"17411","Haddathana Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, akhbarana Ibn Ajlan from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah from Mahmud ibn Labid from Rafi ibn Khadij who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Pray Fajr in brightness for it is greater for the reward."
"17412","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyaynah who said I heard Amr who said Ibn Umar heard, he said We used to sharecrop and saw no harm in that until Rafi claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it, so we left it."
"17413","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from Rafi ibn Khadij who said I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say There is no amputation for fruit nor for palm pith."
"17414","Haddathana al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad from Abd al-Wahid ibn Nafi al-Kalai of the people of Basrah who said I passed by a mosque in Madinah and the prayer was established, and there was an old man who blamed the muadhdhin and said Did you not know that my father told me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order delaying this prayer. He said I said Who is this old man. They said This is Abdullah ibn Rafi ibn Khadij."
"17415","Haddathana Said ibn Amir who said haddathana Shubah who said haddathana Said ibn Masruq from Abayah ibn Rifaa ibn Rafi ibn Khadij from his grandfather Rafi ibn Khadij who said I said O Messenger of Allah, we shall meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives with us. He said Whatever causes blood to flow and the name of Allah is mentioned over it, eat, except tooth and nail, and I shall tell you, as for tooth it is bone, and as for nail it is the knives of the Abyssinians. He said And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seized booty and a camel fled from it, so they chased it and could not catch it, then a man shot it with an arrow and restrained it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said These camels, or he said livestock, have wildness like the wildness of wild animals, so whatever overcomes you, do with it thus."
"17416","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said who said haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman from Hanzalah al-Zuraqi from Rafi ibn Khadij that the people used to lease farms in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the water channels and what the spring waters and something of straw, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disliked leasing farms for this and forbade it. Rafi said There is no harm in leasing them for dirhams and dinars."
"17417","Haddathana Yaqub who said haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq who said haddathani Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah al-Ansari from Mahmud ibn Labid from Rafi ibn Khadij al-Ansari who said I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say The worker on charity in truth is like a warrior in the path of Allah until he returns to his house."
"17418","Haddathana Asbat ibn Muhammad, haddathana Hisham ibn Sad from Zayd ibn Aslam from Mahmud ibn Labid from one of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Pray Fajr in brightness for it is greater for the reward."
"17419","Haddathana Yaqub who said haddathana Abu Uways Abdullah ibn Abdullah from al-Zuhri who said I asked Salim ibn Abdullah about leasing farms, so he said Akhbarani Abdullah ibn Umar from Rafi ibn Khadij that his two uncles, who had both witnessed Badr, told him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade leasing farms."
"17420","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said who said haddathana Rishdin ibn Sad from Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi from one of the sons of Rafi ibn Khadij from Rafi ibn Khadij who said The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me while I was on my wife, so I rose without ejaculating, then bathed and went out to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him that you called me while I was on my wife, so I rose without ejaculating and bathed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said No harm on you, water is from water. Rafi said Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after that ordered us to bathe."
"17421","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Musab, haddathana al-Awzai from Abu al-Najashi from Rafi ibn Khadij who said We used to pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then slaughter a camel and divide it into ten parts, then cook and eat ripe meat before we prayed Maghrib."
"17422","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, haddathana Ayyub ibn Utbah, haddathana Ata Abu al-Najashi who said haddathana Rafi ibn Khadij who said My uncle Zuhayr ibn Rafi met me and said O son of my brother, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us a matter that was beneficial to us. He said So I said What is it, O uncle. He said He forbade us to lease our mahqil, meaning our land at Sirar. He said I said O uncle, obedience to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is more due. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Then you lease them. He said With the streams and with sa measures of barley. He said So do not do so, cultivate them or give them to cultivate. He said So we sold our properties at Sirar. Abdullah said And I asked my father about the hadiths of Rafi ibn Khadij, sometimes saying the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us and sometimes saying from his two uncles, so he said All of them are sound and the most beloved of them to me is the hadith of Ayyub."
